      "text": [
        " :\nسَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ يَمُوتُ وَ يَتْرُكُ اِبْناً مَمْلُوكاً قَالَ \"يُشْتَرَى اِبْنُهُ مِنْ مَالِهِ فَيُعْتَقُ وَ يُوَرَّثُ مَا بَقِيَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5733 - Muhammad ibn Abi Umayr narrated from Jameel who said:\nI asked Abu Abdullah Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about a man who dies and leaves behind a son who is enslaved.\nImam (as) said: \"His son should be purchased from his wealth, then freed, and he will inherit whatever remains.\""
        ]
      }
